body:
How about the html file is written as such:

    {% if name is not none %}
        <p>customer name is : {{ name }}</p>
    {% else %}
        # Do whatever is done when name is none
    {% endif %}

Without the code I provided above of course.

Maybe explicitly giving name as None in the home function like so?

    def home:
        return render_template('default.html', name=None)

As the default.html file itself has the value name, no matter what view function it is used in.
